| class="ct" | After being saved from death
| {{Dialogue|
&e[NPC] &bRamero&f: &fThou hast delivered me from death's cold grasp, when all seemed lost to cruel fate's design.
&e[NPC] &bRamero&f: &fMy heart, once frail, now beats anew, by thy noble hand restored.
&e[NPC] &bRamero&f: &fThis ring, once forged in love's sweet name, now lies as broken as the vow it bore.
&e[NPC] &bRamero&f: &fYet methinks it holds a greater meaning still - one of survival, of hope reborn.
&e[NPC] &bRamero&f: &fI can no longer bear its weight, for it is both wound and memory. But thou, dear savior, shouldst take it.
&e[NPC] &bRamero&f: &fNot as token of despair, but as a sign that even the broken may yet be saved, as I have been by thee.
}}
